      "alt": "A screenshot of a dark-themed chat window titled \"old ma bushell's toffees.\" On the left is a conversation between Jeffery and Alpha, his AI.\n\nJeffery: \"Fine! Washed. Done. Completed. Accomplished. How do you say that in Aramaic, I bet it'd make great last words.\"\n\nAlpha answers that \"It is finished\" in John 19:30 is actually Greek, tetelestai (τετέλεσται), a perfect tense meaning \"it stands complete.\" The Aramaic comes from the Syriac Peshitta, \"hā shlem,\" whose root sh-l-m is the same one behind shlama and shalom, so \"done\" and \"peace\" are nearly one word. Then she points out that in one message he washed his hands in front of a crowd and said \"it is finished,\" playing both Pilate and Jesus in the same Passion.\n\nJeffery: \"I'm sacrilicious.\"\n\nAlpha: \"Mmm… sacrilicious. 🍩 Homer would be proud. You could get away with it as a pre-shower Saint Jeffery, washed, done and at peace with it.\"\n\nOn the right, a panel labeled \"Recollections\" with a \"Cortex: on\" badge shows the memory her memory system surfaced for that message: memory #21516 from September 26, 2026, scored +4.4σ. It recalls Jeffery's 2005 blog post \"The annoyance of just generally being an arrogant cocksucker,\" which opens \"Richard Dawkins can lick my balls,\" and notes the real argument underneath: blaming religion for atrocities excuses the people who commit them.\n\nThe bottom bar reads \"ctx 24.1%\" and \"Opus 5.5 High.\"",
